# Settings: the tools each page talks to.
#   Sound (pactl), battery and power (power profiles, brightness), users (AccountsService), VPN files (OpenVPN;
#   WireGuard is built into NetworkManager), and the radio switch for airplane mode (rfkill, from util-linux).
pulseaudio-utils
power-profiles-daemon
upower
brightnessctl
accountsservice
network-manager-openvpn
util-linux
pciutils
# Software Update: PackageKit for system updates (and offline updates at restart), fwupd for firmware.
packagekit
# (pkcon came in packagekit-tools; PackageKit 1.3 puts pkgcli in packagekit itself)
# The App Store's other source: Ubuntu's own packages of the apps it lists from Flathub, found in Ubuntu's AppStream
# catalogue, which apt fetches with the package lists once this is installed (apps/huginn_debapps.py).
appstream
fwupd
# Photos editing and Easel: numpy and Pillow do the picture work; Qt SVG writes SVG.
python3-numpy
python3-pil
python3-pyside6.qtsvg
# Accessibility: the screen reader and its voice, and an on-screen keyboard (KWin's zoom, colour filters and
# keyboard helps are built in).
orca
speech-dispatcher
espeak-ng
maliit-keyboard
# Displays: the brightness of screens plugged in by a cable (DDC/CI: most monitors), as laptops' own screens have
ddcutil
# Appearance › Icons and Pointer: a few more to choose from (besides Huginn's own, Breeze and Adwaita)
elementary-icon-theme
dmz-cursor-theme
oxygen-cursor-theme
